From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] avcodec/vc1dec: honour AV_CODEC_FLAG_LOW_DELAY

The decoder held each I- and P-picture back until the next one, for
display order, whatever the caller asked. With AV_CODEC_FLAG_LOW_DELAY
it now hands every picture out once decoded, as the MPEG-1/2 and
MPEG-4 Part 2 decoders already do, so a low-latency caller gets the
same behaviour across the codecs.
---
diff --git a/libavcodec/vc1dec.c b/libavcodec/vc1dec.c
--- a/libavcodec/vc1dec.c
+++ b/libavcodec/vc1dec.c
@@ -1014,7 +1014,8 @@
         if (ret < 0)
             goto err;
 
-        s->low_delay = !avctx->has_b_frames || v->res_sprite;
+        s->low_delay = !avctx->has_b_frames || v->res_sprite ||
+                       (avctx->flags & AV_CODEC_FLAG_LOW_DELAY);
 
         if (v->profile == PROFILE_ADVANCED) {
             if(avctx->coded_width<=1 || avctx->coded_height<=1) {
